PROOF-CARRIER TOURNAMENT
========================
Pairwise observable: majority vote over
  forward_primes, reverse_irreducibility, recombination, support_retention, repo_bridge
Tie path: lower risk, then declaration/name.
  bunyakovsky_forward_atom: score=0, metrics=(5,1,1,2,4; risk=5)
    note: irreducible primitive f should hit infinitely many primes
  singh_murty_value_factor_bound: score=7, metrics=(2,5,2,4,5; risk=1)
    note: large value plus prime factorization bounds irreducible factors
  cohn_digit_prime_certificate: score=4, metrics=(2,5,1,3,4; risk=1)
    note: base-b digits of prime N give irreducible digit polynomial
  iravanian_real_trace_recombination: score=2, metrics=(1,3,5,4,4; risk=2)
    note: factor over R, then solve integer trace/subset constraints
  finite_field_hensel_recombination: score=2, metrics=(1,4,4,3,3; risk=1)
    note: standard modular factor-lift-recombine pipeline
  newton_nonarch_bivariate_gate: score=3, metrics=(1,4,2,5,4; risk=2)
    note: Singh bivariate/non-Archimedean extension keeps degree support
  local_fixed_divisor_sieve: score=4, metrics=(4,2,1,4,5; risk=2)
    note: fixed divisor / local obstruction is Bunyakovsky's admissibility gate
  repo_support_gate_LRC72: score=6, metrics=(2,3,2,5,5; risk=2)
    note: same scalar/support split seen in LRC14 and [72,36,16]
